      },
      {
        "id": "f2_cond",
        "masters": [
          "{F_CEILINGS}"
        ],
        "sub": "{F2_CONDITION}",
        "text": "Condition: Where visible, the ceilings appear in {CEILING_CONDITION} condition, consistent with their age and construction. No defects noted: No significant defects requiring immediate attention were identified unless otherwise stated below. Routine maintenance appropriate to the ceiling material should be expected.",
        "tokens": [
          {
            "kind": "dropdown",
            "token": "{CEILING_CONDITION}",
            "dropdown": "actv_condition",
            "field_label": "Condition",
            "dropdown_options": [
              "Good",
              "Reasonable",
              "Fair",
              "Poor",
              "Very poor"
            ],
            "pdf_options": [
              "good",
              "reasonable",
              "fair",
              "poor",
              "very poor"
            ],
            "lower": true
          }
        ],
        "pdf": [
          "Condition: Where visible, the ceilings appear in good, reasonable, fair, poor, very poor condition, consistent with their age and construction."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f2_lath",
        "masters": [
          "{F_CEILINGS}"
        ],
        "sub": "{F2_LATH_PLASTER}",
        "text": "The ceilings are fully or partially made of older plaster supported on thin wooden strips (called ‘lath and plaster’), typical of properties built before the 1940s. While no significant defects were noted at the time of inspection, these ceilings can deteriorate with age as the plaster loses its bond with the timber laths. They are susceptible to vibration and disturbance, and localised repairs are likely to be required over time, particularly during redecoration or alteration works. Repairs can be difficult and may dislodge adjacent plaster, making complete ceiling replacement more economical in some cases.",
        "tokens": [],
        "when": [
          "f2m_lath_and_plaster",
          "true"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f2_textured",
        "masters": [
          "{F_CEILINGS}"
        ],
        "sub": "{F2_TEXTURED_COATING}",
        "text": "Parts of the ceilings within the property may contain asbestos-containing materials. In their current condition, these are not normally considered a significant risk if left undisturbed. However, they should not be drilled, sanded, cut, or otherwise disturbed without appropriate precautions. If future refurbishment or replacement is planned, the material should be assessed beforehand and, if asbestos is confirmed, removed by a licensed contractor. This can add significantly to the cost of future works.",
        "tokens": [],
        "when": [
          "f2f_textured_coating",
          "true"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f2_general",
        "masters": [
          "{F_CEILINGS}"
        ],
        "sub": "{F2_GENERAL_MAINTENANCE}",
        "text": "General Maintenance: Ceilings should be inspected periodically for signs of cracking, distortion, or water penetration. Prompt repair of roof leaks, plumbing defects and condensation problems will reduce the likelihood of damage to internal ceiling finishes. Routine redecoration should be expected throughout the normal life of the property.",
        "tokens": [],
        "when": [
          "cb_general_maintenance",
          "true"
        ],
        "extra_fields": [
          {
            "id": "cb_general_maintenance",
            "label": "General maintenance",
            "type": "checkbox"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
